IMPORT prelude

-- Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (Western Australia) -- who decides whether my tissue is taken after I die (Part 3:
-- ss 22, 23, 24, 24A, with the s 3(1) definitions of child, next of kin and senior available next of kin); what must be shown
-- before tissue is taken from a body kept breathing by machine (s 24(2), (3)); giving tissue or blood while I am alive, as an
-- adult or as a child (Part 2: ss 8, 9, 11-20); selling tissue (ss 29, 29A); and whether my identity as a donor may be
-- disclosed (s 34).
--
-- SEAT: the potential donor (while living, and as the person whose body it is after death) and the senior available next of
-- kin. Every decision is phrased as one of them would ask it: "Whose consent governs donation of my organs?", "Can my family
-- override my consent?", "Am I the senior available next of kin?", "Does my objection stop it?", "May I give a kidney while I
-- am alive?", "May my child give bone marrow?", "Is my agreement to sell tissue void?". The Act addresses the designated
-- officer of a hospital; what it means for the donor is what may be done to their body. Where the Act hands a judgment to the
-- designated officer ("is satisfied", "has reason to believe"), the coroner, the Minister or a medical practitioner, that
-- judgment is asked as a fact, never guessed.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) ("child", "next of kin", "nonregenerative tissue", "regenerative tissue", "senior available next
-- of kin", "tissue"), s 8, s 9, s 11, s 12, s 13, s 14, s 15, s 16, s 17, s 18, s 19, s 20, s 22(1)-(5), s 23(1), (2), s 24(1),
-- (1A), (1B), (2), (3), s 24A(1), (2), s 29, s 29A(2), (3), (4), s 29C(4), s 29D(1), (2), s 29E(2), s 34.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49110, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49110.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table runs to the
-- Therapeutic Goods Law Application Act 2024 Pt 8 Div 1 (No. 19 of 2024, in operation 30 August 2024); the last reprint it
-- lists is Reprint 3 as at 19 May 2017; Part 16 of the Assisted Reproductive Technology and Surrogacy Act 2025 is listed as
-- uncommenced and is not reflected. No regulations set a number the encoded provisions use: the only numbers are the age of
-- 18, the 24 hours (ss 9, 16), the 2 practitioners and 5 years (s 24(2)), and the s 29A(3) penalty, all in the Act.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: designated officers, delegation and the Minister's delegation (ss 4, 5, 5A); s 21 (an emergency transfusion
-- on a child -- the child is the recipient, not a donor); s 23(3), (4) (conditions on and the form of a coroner's consent);
-- s 24A(3), (4); Part 4 (postmortem examinations); s 29A(4)(b)-(f), ss 29B, 29C, 29D(1) and 29E in detail (each is one
-- fact); s 29F (the Advisory Body); s 30 (advertising); Part 6 (embryonic stem cell lines); ss 31, 32, 32A, 32B, 33 (liability,
-- the procedures the Act does not touch, codes of practice and offences by those who remove tissue); ss 35, 37. The
-- Australian Organ Donor Register is a Commonwealth register: THE DEPOSITED TEXT DOES NOT MENTION IT. Treating a registration
-- as the deceased's having "expressed the wish for, or consented to, the removal after death of tissue" (s 22(2)(a)) is an
-- INFERENCE. The Act has NO DEFINITION OF DEATH: the only rule on brain death is s 24(2), a precondition to removal from a
-- ventilated body.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA)`

§§ `numbers the Act sets`

-- s 3(1): "child means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years"; ss 8(1)(a), 9(1)(a), 18(1)(a): "has attained the
-- age of 18 years".
`the age of adulthood` MEANS 18

-- ss 9(1), 16: "after the expiration of a period of 24 hours from the time at which the consent is signed".
`the waiting period in hours` MEANS 24

-- s 24(2): "each of whom has been for a period of not less than 5 years a medical practitioner".
`the years of practice a declaring practitioner needs` MEANS 5

§§ `3(1) -- child, next of kin, senior available next of kin`

-- s 3(1): "next of kin -- (a) in relation to a child, means a person referred to in paragraph (a)(i), (ia), (ii), (iii) or
-- (iv) of the definition of 'senior available next of kin'; and (b) in relation to a person other than a child, ... paragraph
-- (b)(i), (ia), (ii), (iii), or (iv)".
-- "senior available next of kin -- (a) in relation to a child, means the first in order of priority of the following persons
-- who is available at the time -- (i) if the child has both a spouse, and a de facto partner who has attained the age of 18
-- years, the spouse or de facto partner with whom the child is living as a spouse or de facto partner; (ia) the spouse, or de
-- facto partner who has attained the age of 18 years, of the child; (ii) a parent of the child; (iii) a brother or sister, who
-- has attained the age of 18 years, of the child; (iv) a guardian of the child; and (b) in relation to a person other than a
-- child ... (i) [as above]; (ia) [as above]; (ii) a son or daughter, who has attained the age of 18 years, of the person;
-- (iii) a parent of the person; (iv) a brother or sister, who has attained the age of 18 years, of the person".
-- A former spouse, a grandchild, a friend and (for an adult) a guardian appear nowhere in the list. "Spouse", "de facto
-- partner", "parent" and "available" are borrowed or undefined terms, asked as facts.
DECLARE Kinship IS ONE OF
    `spouse`
    `de facto partner`
    `former spouse`
    `son or daughter`
    `parent`
    `brother or sister`
    `guardian`
    `another relative or friend`

-- `consents to the removal` means consent to the removal of THIS tissue for THIS purpose (s 22(3)(b) restricts the authority
-- "both as to the tissue which may be removed and as to the purpose or use of the tissue").
DECLARE Relative HAS
    `kinship` IS A Kinship
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `is available at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lives with the deceased as a spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consents to the removal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `objects to the removal` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 24(2): "2 medical practitioners (each of whom has carried out a clinical examination of the person, each of whom has been
-- for a period of not less than 5 years a medical practitioner and one of whom holds specialist qualifications in general
-- medicine, neurology or neurosurgery or has such other qualifications as are accepted by the Chief Health Officer)".
-- s 24(3): practice "under the law in force in a country outside Australia must be taken into account" in the 5 years.
DECLARE Practitioner HAS
    `has carried out a clinical examination of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years as a medical practitioner, in Australia or overseas` IS A NUMBER
    `holds specialist qualifications in general medicine, neurology or neurosurgery, or others the Chief Health Officer accepts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared that irreversible cessation of all function of the brain has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts about the person who has died. Fields marked (officer) are the designated officer's judgment "after making
-- inquiries" (s 22(2)), or the officer's "reason to believe" (s 23(1)), asked as facts.
DECLARE Deceased HAS
    `age at death` IS A NUMBER
    `died in a hospital or was brought into one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `expressed a wish for, or consented to, removal after death, not withdrawn (officer)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tissue and purpose sought are within the terms of that wish or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `expressed an objection to removal after death (officer has reason to believe)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death is or may be a reportable death (officer has reason to believe)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the coroner consented, or directed that consent is not required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `respiration and circulation are maintained by artificial means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the declaring practitioners` IS A LIST OF Practitioner
    `relatives` IS A LIST OF Relative

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deceased was a child` d IF d's `age at death` LESS THAN `the age of adulthood`

GIVEN r IS A Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spouse or adult de facto partner` r IF
        r's `kinship` EQUALS `spouse`
    OR  (r's `kinship` EQUALS `de facto partner` AND r's `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood`)

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a spouse is among` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r's `kinship` EQUALS `spouse` OR `a spouse is among` rest

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an adult de facto partner is among` rs MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (r's `kinship` EQUALS `de facto partner` AND r's `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood`)
        OR  `an adult de facto partner is among` rest

-- Paragraph (i): "if the person HAS both a spouse, and a de facto partner who has attained the age of 18 years". Read as all
-- the relatives, available or not.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has both a spouse and an adult de facto partner` d IF
    `a spouse is among` (d's `relatives`) AND `an adult de facto partner is among` (d's `relatives`)

-- The subparagraph a relative falls in, numbered 1 to 5 for (i), (ia), (ii), (iii), (iv); 0 if in none.
-- Under (i), the partner the person is NOT living with drops out of (i) but still falls under (ia) (READING: (ia) is not
-- made subject to (i)).
GIVEN r IS A Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the subparagraph of the relative` r d MEANS
    IF `is a spouse or adult de facto partner` r
    THEN IF `has both a spouse and an adult de facto partner` d AND r's `lives with the deceased as a spouse or de facto partner`
         THEN 1
         ELSE 2
    ELSE IF `the deceased was a child` d
         THEN CONSIDER r's `kinship`
              WHEN `parent` THEN 3
              WHEN `brother or sister` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood` THEN 4 ELSE 0
              WHEN `guardian` THEN 5
              OTHERWISE 0
         ELSE CONSIDER r's `kinship`
              WHEN `son or daughter` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood` THEN 3 ELSE 0
              WHEN `parent` THEN 4
              WHEN `brother or sister` THEN IF r's `age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood` THEN 5 ELSE 0
              OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher priority` a b MEANS
    IF a EQUALS 0 THEN b
    ELSE IF b EQUALS 0 THEN a
         ELSE IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest priority available among` rs d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the higher priority`
            (IF r's `is available at the time` THEN `the subparagraph of the relative` r d ELSE 0)
            (`the highest priority available among` rest d)

-- "the first in order of priority ... who is available at the time"; 0 means no one is.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the senior subparagraph` d MEANS `the highest priority available among` (d's `relatives`) d

@export Am I next of kin of the person, under the Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 3(1)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age and what you say
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, and their family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I next of kin` `me` `the person` IF `the subparagraph of the relative` `me` `the person` GREATER THAN 0

@export Am I the senior available next of kin of the person (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 3(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person, your age and whether you are available
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person whose tissue is in question, and their family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the senior available next of kin` `me` `the person` IF
        `me`'s `is available at the time`
    AND `the senior subparagraph` `the person` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the subparagraph of the relative` `me` `the person` EQUALS `the senior subparagraph` `the person`

§§ `22(2)(b), (5) -- the senior available next of kin consents`

-- s 22(5): "Where there are 2 or more persons having a description referred to in a subparagraph of paragraph (a) or (b) of the
-- definition of 'senior available next of kin' in section 3, an objection by any one of those persons has effect for the
-- purposes of this section notwithstanding any indication to the contrary by the other or any other of those persons."
-- READING: one objection within the senior description defeats the others' consent; an objection from a LOWER description
-- has no effect; (5) does not ask whether the objector is "available". The text rules none of these.
GIVEN r IS A Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is of the senior description` r d IF
        `the senior subparagraph` d GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the subparagraph of the relative` r d EQUALS `the senior subparagraph` d

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a senior available next of kin among` rs `consents` d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (`Am I the senior available next of kin` r d AND r's `consents to the removal`)
        OR  `a senior available next of kin among` rest `consents` d

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF Relative
      d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`someone of the senior description among` rs `objects` d MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (`is of the senior description` r d AND r's `objects to the removal`)
        OR  `someone of the senior description among` rest `objects` d

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the senior available next of kin consents` d IF
        `a senior available next of kin among` (d's `relatives`) `consents` d
    AND (NOT `someone of the senior description among` (d's `relatives`) `objects` d)

§§ `22(1), (2), (3) -- the designated officer may authorise removal`

-- s 22(2): the officer may authorise removal from the body of a person who has died in, or been brought into, the hospital --
-- "(a) where, after making inquiries, the designated officer is satisfied that the deceased person during the person's
-- lifetime expressed the wish for, or consented to, the removal after death of tissue ... and had not withdrawn the wish or
-- revoked the consent; or (b) where, after making inquiries, the designated officer has no reason to believe that the deceased
-- person had expressed an objection ... and the designated officer is satisfied that the senior available next of kin
-- consents".
-- s 22(3): restricted "(a) ... by the expressed terms of the wishes or consent of the deceased person; (b) ... by the consent of
-- the senior available next of kin, both as to the tissue which may be removed and as to the purpose or use of the tissue".
-- There is no third limb: donation is not presumed. Paragraph (a) says nothing about the family. Part 3 sets no minimum age
-- for the deceased's own wish.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (a) is met` d IF
        d's `died in a hospital or was brought into one`
    AND d's `expressed a wish for, or consented to, removal after death, not withdrawn (officer)`
    AND d's `the tissue and purpose sought are within the terms of that wish or consent`

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (b) is met` d IF
        d's `died in a hospital or was brought into one`
    AND (NOT d's `expressed an objection to removal after death (officer has reason to believe)`)
    AND `the senior available next of kin consents` d

§§ `23 -- the coroner's consent for a reportable death`

-- s 23(1): "If the designated officer for a hospital has reason to believe that the death of a person is or may be a reportable
-- death, the designated officer must not, under and in accordance with section 22, authorise the removal of tissue ... unless
-- the coroner has given consent to the removal." (2): a coroner may direct, before or after death, that consent is not required.
GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 23 bars the authority` d IF
        d's `the death is or may be a reportable death (officer has reason to believe)`
    AND (NOT d's `the coroner consented, or directed that consent is not required`)

DECLARE `Whose consent governs` IS ONE OF
    `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
    `my senior available next of kin's consent (s 22(2)(b))`
    `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
    `no one's: there is no authority to remove my tissue`

@export Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23)?
GIVEN `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes and your family
GIVETH A `Whose consent governs`
DECIDE `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `me` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT `paragraph (a) is met` `me`) AND (NOT `paragraph (b) is met` `me`)
        THEN `no one's: there is no authority to remove my tissue`
      IF `section 23 bars the authority` `me`
        THEN `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
      IF `paragraph (a) is met` `me`
        THEN `my own wish or consent, which no one else's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
      OTHERWISE `my senior available next of kin's consent (s 22(2)(b))`

GIVEN d IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designated officer may authorise the removal` d IF
        (`paragraph (a) is met` d OR `paragraph (b) is met` d)
    AND (NOT `section 23 bars the authority` d)

@export Can my next of kin's objection stop removal of tissue from my body after I die (s 22(2), (5))?
GIVEN `my relative` IS A Relative @desc The relative who objects
      `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes and your family
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my relative's objection stop the removal` `my relative` `me` IF
        `my relative`'s `objects to the removal`
    AND (NOT `paragraph (a) is met` `me`)
    AND `is of the senior description` `my relative` `me`

§§ `22(4) -- the next of kin's consent while the person is unconscious`

-- s 22(4): the senior available next of kin may make known, "at any time when the person is unconscious before death", consent
-- to removal after death, "but the designated officer must not act on such an indication if the person recovers consciousness".
@export May the officer act on the consent I gave as senior next of kin while the person was unconscious (s 22(4))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Relative @desc Who you are to the person
      `the person` IS A Deceased @desc The person, and their family
      `the person recovered consciousness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person recovered consciousness after you gave your consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my consent given during unconsciousness be acted on` `me` `the person` `the person recovered consciousness` IF
        `Am I the senior available next of kin` `me` `the person`
    AND `me`'s `consents to the removal`
    AND (NOT `the person recovered consciousness`)

§§ `24(2), (3) -- a body kept breathing by artificial means`

-- s 24(2): "Where the respiration and the circulation of the blood of a person are being maintained by artificial means, tissue
-- must not be removed from the body of the person for a permitted purpose or use unless 2 medical practitioners ... have declared
-- that irreversible cessation of all function of the brain of the person has occurred."
-- The Act defines no "death". This is the only rule on brain death in the deposit, and it is a precondition to removal.
GIVEN p IS A Practitioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualifying declarer` p IF
        p's `has carried out a clinical examination of the person`
    AND p's `years as a medical practitioner, in Australia or overseas` AT LEAST `the years of practice a declaring practitioner needs`
    AND p's `declared that irreversible cessation of all function of the brain has occurred`

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Practitioner
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of qualifying declarers among` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF `is a qualifying declarer` p THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `the number of qualifying declarers among` rest

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF Practitioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a qualifying declarer is a specialist among` ps MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (`is a qualifying declarer` p AND p's `holds specialist qualifications in general medicine, neurology or neurosurgery, or others the Chief Health Officer accepts`)
        OR  `a qualifying declarer is a specialist among` rest

@export Have the brain-death declarations section 24(2) requires been made about me (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 24(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the declarers` IS A LIST OF Practitioner @desc The medical practitioners who examined you and what they declared
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the section 24(2) declarations been made` `the declarers` IF
        `the number of qualifying declarers among` `the declarers` AT LEAST 2
    AND `a qualifying declarer is a specialist among` `the declarers`

@export May tissue be removed from my body after I die (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 22, 23, 24(2))?
GIVEN `me` IS A Deceased @desc The facts of your death, your recorded wishes, your family and any brain-death declarations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my tissue be removed after my death` `me` IF
        `the designated officer may authorise the removal` `me`
    AND (    (NOT `me`'s `respiration and circulation are maintained by artificial means`)
         OR  `Have the section 24(2) declarations been made` (`me`'s `the declaring practitioners`))

§§ `24(1), (1A), 24A(2) -- who may remove the tissue`

-- s 24(1): "permitted practitioner ... means a medical practitioner other than -- (a) if subsection (2) applies -- a medical
-- practitioner who made a declaration under that subsection relating to the authority; or (b) the designated officer for the
-- hospital ... or a person who has lawfully exercised the designated officer's powers under section 22".
-- s 24(1A): ocular tissue, musculoskeletal tissue and skin may be removed by a permitted practitioner or a person appointed
-- under s 24A(1) for that paragraph; "(d) in any other case -- a permitted practitioner". s 24A(2): "A person cannot be an
-- authorised person if the person is a medical practitioner."
DECLARE `Tissue after death` IS ONE OF
    `ocular tissue`
    `musculoskeletal tissue`
    `skin`
    `other tissue, such as a kidney`

DECLARE Remover HAS
    `is a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a section 24(2) declaration about the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the designated officer, or exercised the officer's powers under s 22` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is appointed under s 24A(1) as an authorised person for this kind of tissue` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN w IS A Remover
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a permitted practitioner` w IF
        w's `is a medical practitioner`
    AND (NOT w's `made a section 24(2) declaration about the deceased`)
    AND (NOT w's `is the designated officer, or exercised the officer's powers under s 22`)

@export May this person remove this tissue from my body under the authority (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 24(1), (1A), 24A(2))?
GIVEN `the remover` IS A Remover @desc Who would remove the tissue
      `the tissue` IS A `Tissue after death` @desc The kind of tissue
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person remove my tissue` `the remover` `the tissue` IF
        `is a permitted practitioner` `the remover`
    OR  (    (NOT `the remover`'s `is a medical practitioner`)
         AND `the remover`'s `is appointed under s 24A(1) as an authorised person for this kind of tissue`
         AND (NOT (`the tissue` EQUALS `other tissue, such as a kidney`)))

§§ `8, 9, 18 -- giving tissue or blood while I am alive, as an adult`

-- s 3(1): "regenerative tissue means tissue that, after injury or removal, is replaced in the body of a living person by
-- natural processes of growth or repair"; "nonregenerative tissue means tissue other than regenerative tissue".
-- s 6: in Part 2, tissue does not include "fetal tissue, a human embryo, human sperm or a human egg".
DECLARE `Living tissue` IS ONE OF
    `regenerative tissue other than blood, such as bone marrow`
    `nonregenerative tissue, such as a kidney`
    `blood`

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `transplantation to another living person`
    `other therapeutic, medical or scientific use`
    `training, education or quality assurance for such a use`

-- s 8(1): a person who "(a) has attained the age of 18 years; and (b) is of sound mind; and (c) is, in the light of medical
-- advice furnished to the person, prepared to consent" may "(1A) ... by writing signed by the person otherwise than in the
-- presence of any member of the person's family or any of the person's friends, consent to the removal ... of regenerative
-- tissue, other than blood" for transplantation, other therapeutic, medical or scientific purposes, or training.
-- s 9(1): the same four conditions, for "nonregenerative tissue ... for the purpose of the transplantation of the tissue to the
-- body of another living person" only.
-- s 18: a person who "(a) has attained the age of 18 years; and (b) is of sound mind" may consent to the removal of blood for
-- transfusion or the other uses -- no writing, no medical advice. A transfusion to another person is entered as
-- `transplantation to another living person`.
-- For a child, see ss 12, 13, 19 below: a child cannot consent for themselves.
DECLARE `My consent` HAS
    `my age` IS A NUMBER
    `I am of sound mind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am prepared to consent in the light of medical advice given to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I signed it in writing, away from my family and friends` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May I consent to giving this tissue for this purpose while I am alive (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 8, 9, 18)?
GIVEN `the consent` IS A `My consent` @desc Your age and how you consent
      `the tissue` IS A `Living tissue` @desc The tissue you would give
      `the purpose` IS A Purpose @desc What the tissue is for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I consent to giving this tissue while I am alive` `the consent` `the tissue` `the purpose` IF
        `the consent`'s `my age` AT LEAST `the age of adulthood`
    AND `the consent`'s `I am of sound mind`
    AND CONSIDER `the tissue`
        WHEN `blood` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `regenerative tissue other than blood, such as bone marrow` THEN
                `the consent`'s `I am prepared to consent in the light of medical advice given to me`
            AND `the consent`'s `I signed it in writing, away from my family and friends`
        WHEN `nonregenerative tissue, such as a kidney` THEN
                `the consent`'s `I am prepared to consent in the light of medical advice given to me`
            AND `the consent`'s `I signed it in writing, away from my family and friends`
            AND `the purpose` EQUALS `transplantation to another living person`

§§ `8(2), 9(2), 15, 16, 20 -- when my consent lets the tissue be taken`

-- s 15: a s 8 consent "is, unless it has been revoked under section 8(2), sufficient authority for a medical practitioner, other
-- than a medical practitioner by whom the medical advice ... was furnished, to remove the regenerative tissue".
-- s 16: a s 9 consent, unless revoked, is sufficient authority for such a practitioner "to remove, after the expiration of a
-- period of 24 hours after the time at which the consent was given, the nonregenerative tissue". Removal at exactly 24 hours is
-- read as NOT after the expiration (READING).
-- ss 8(2), 9(2): revocable "at any time before the removal ..., either orally or in writing".
-- s 20: a blood consent "is sufficient authority for the removal of blood" -- no waiting period and no exclusion of the adviser.
-- The Act gives no revocation rule for blood; a revoked blood consent is treated as no consent (INFERENCE).
@export May my tissue be removed now under the consent I gave while alive (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 8(2), 9(2), 15, 16, 20)?
GIVEN `the tissue` IS A `Living tissue` @desc The tissue you consented to give
      `hours since I signed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours have passed since you signed the consent
      `I revoked my consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have revoked the consent, orally or in writing
      `the remover gave me the medical advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner who would remove it is the one who advised you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my tissue be removed now under my consent` `the tissue` `hours since I signed` `I revoked my consent` `the remover gave me the medical advice` IF
        (NOT `I revoked my consent`)
    AND CONSIDER `the tissue`
        WHEN `blood` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `regenerative tissue other than blood, such as bone marrow` THEN (NOT `the remover gave me the medical advice`)
        WHEN `nonregenerative tissue, such as a kidney` THEN
                (NOT `the remover gave me the medical advice`)
            AND `hours since I signed` GREATER THAN `the waiting period in hours`

§§ `11, 12, 13, 14, 17, 19 -- tissue or blood from a living child`

-- s 12(2): "It is not lawful to remove nonregenerative tissue from the body of a living child for the purpose of the
-- transplantation of the tissue to the body of another living person." (1): regenerative tissue only "as provided by this Part".
-- s 13: a parent may consent in writing to removal of specified regenerative tissue "for the purpose of the transplantation of
-- the tissue to the body of another member of the family of the child or to the body of a relative of the child" where "(a)
-- medical advice has been furnished to the parent and the child ...; (b) the child has the mental capacity to understand ...;
-- and (c) the child has agreed". s 11: a parent "does not include ... the guardian of a child or ... another person standing in
-- loco parentis". s 14: the parent or the child may revoke before removal. s 17: the consent is then sufficient authority.
-- s 19: a parent may consent to removal of blood from the child if "(a) a medical practitioner advises that the removal should
-- not be prejudicial to the health of the child; and (b) the child agrees".
DECLARE `My child's donation` HAS
    `the tissue` IS A `Living tissue`
    `consent given by a parent, not a guardian or other person in loco parentis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent's consent is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for transplantation to a member of the child's family or a relative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical advice was given to the parent and the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child can understand the removal and the transplantation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent or the child revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a medical practitioner advises the removal should not harm the child's health` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May tissue or blood be taken from my child, who is under 18, for another person (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 11-14, 17, 19)?
GIVEN `the donation` IS A `My child's donation` @desc The tissue, who consents and what your child understands and agrees to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May tissue be taken from my child` `the donation` IF
    CONSIDER `the donation`'s `the tissue`
    WHEN `nonregenerative tissue, such as a kidney` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `regenerative tissue other than blood, such as bone marrow` THEN
            `the donation`'s `consent given by a parent, not a guardian or other person in loco parentis`
        AND `the donation`'s `the parent's consent is in writing`
        AND `the donation`'s `for transplantation to a member of the child's family or a relative`
        AND `the donation`'s `medical advice was given to the parent and the child`
        AND `the donation`'s `the child can understand the removal and the transplantation`
        AND `the donation`'s `the child agreed`
        AND (NOT `the donation`'s `the parent or the child revoked`)
    WHEN `blood` THEN
            `the donation`'s `consent given by a parent, not a guardian or other person in loco parentis`
        AND `the donation`'s `a medical practitioner advises the removal should not harm the child's health`
        AND `the donation`'s `the child agreed`

§§ `29, 29A -- selling tissue`

-- s 29A(2): "a contract or arrangement is void if, under the contract or arrangement, a person agrees, for valuable consideration,
-- whether given or to be given to that person or to another person -- (a) to the sale or supply of tissue from that person's body
-- or from the body of another person, whether before or after that person's death ...; or (b) to the postmortem examination or
-- anatomical examination of that person's body after death". It is "Subject to subsection (4) and sections 29C, 29D(1) and 29E".
-- s 29A(4): "Except as provided in section 29D(2), subsection (2) does not apply" to "(a) a contract or arrangement providing only
-- for the reimbursement of any expenses necessarily incurred by a person in relation to the removal of tissue in accordance with
-- this Act" nor to (b)-(f) (listed blood products, exempt entities, approved therapeutic goods, s 29B(3) cost recovery).
-- s 29: the Part does not apply to "the sale or supply of a human embryo, human sperm or a human egg".
-- s 29A(3): "A person who enters into a contract or arrangement of the kind referred to in subsection (2) and to which that
-- subsection applies commits an offence. Penalty for this subsection: imprisonment for 12 months or a fine of $12 000."
DECLARE `What I agree to` IS ONE OF
    `the sale or supply of tissue from my body, before or after my death`
    `the postmortem or anatomical examination of my body after death`
    `the sale or supply of a human embryo, human sperm or a human egg`

DECLARE Deal HAS
    `what I agree to` IS A `What I agree to`
    `for valuable consideration, to me or to another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it only reimburses expenses necessarily incurred in a lawful removal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another exception in s 29A(4)(b)-(f) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Minister's order under s 29D(2) applies s 29A(2) to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 29C, a s 29D(1) order or a s 29E approval takes it outside s 29A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN deal IS A Deal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a subsection (4) exception saves it` deal IF
        (deal's `it only reimburses expenses necessarily incurred in a lawful removal` OR deal's `another exception in s 29A(4)(b)-(f) applies`)
    AND (NOT deal's `a Minister's order under s 29D(2) applies s 29A(2) to it`)

@export Is my agreement to sell my tissue or my body void, and an offence (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) ss 29, 29A(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the deal` IS A Deal @desc What you agreed to, and for what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my agreement void and an offence` `the deal` IF
        (NOT (`the deal`'s `what I agree to` EQUALS `the sale or supply of a human embryo, human sperm or a human egg`))
    AND `the deal`'s `for valuable consideration, to me or to another`
    AND (NOT `a subsection (4) exception saves it` `the deal`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `s 29C, a s 29D(1) order or a s 29E approval takes it outside s 29A(2)`)

DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
    `fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER

@export What is the most I can be punished for entering a void agreement to sell tissue (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 29A(3))?
GIVETH A Penalty
`What is the most I can be punished for trading in tissue` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `months of imprisonment` IS 12
    `fine in dollars` IS 12000

§§ `34 -- may my identity as a donor be disclosed`

-- s 34(1): a person must not disclose information by which the identity of a person "(a) from whose body tissue has been removed
-- for the purpose of transplantation ...; or (b) with respect to whom ... a consent or authority has been given under this Act;
-- or (c) into whose body tissue has been ... transplanted, may become publicly known." Penalty $500.
-- (2): except information disclosed "(a) in pursuance of an order of a Court or when otherwise required by law; or (b) for the
-- purposes of hospital administration or bona fide medical research; or (c) with the consent of the person to whom the
-- information relates; or (d) when ... the disclosure is or would be privileged".
DECLARE `Reason for disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `a court order, or as otherwise required by law`
    `hospital administration or bona fide medical research`
    `with my consent`
    `the disclosure is or would be privileged`
    `none of these`

@export May someone make my identity as a donor or recipient publicly known (Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) s 34)?
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for disclosure` @desc Why the information is disclosed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my identity as a donor be disclosed` `the reason` IF
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
